<title>USA: SmithKline associates survive plane crash.</title>
<headline>SmithKline associates survive plane crash.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>SmithKline Beecham Clinical Laboratories said Thursday that the pilot and copilot of a private airplane owned by the company survived a plane crash at Calhoun Airport outside Atlanta.</p>
<p>Both are SmithKline associates.</p>
<p>According to the company, the plane was carrying diagnostic specimens to its Atlanta laboratory for medical testing.</p>
<p>SmithKline said that company representatives are enroute to collect the specimens from the crash site and that the specimens pose no threat to public safety or health.</p>
</text>
